const agentDescriptions={"AIUTO": "Ask a precise setup question and get the documented procedure for the software already open, without leaving the session.", "PRESTO": "Drafts the reply to a client brief from your saved bio, rates and tone. You review, adjust and send it yourself.", "TEMPO": "Turns a described scene function into temporary audio you can place against the edit and replace with your own cue.", "VOCE": "Drop in the recording of a call, a meeting or a voice note, audio or video, and get back a report: summary, decisions, to do, open questions.", "CECILIA": "Reads the notation on an unlabelled page and names the work, the composer and the context you needed to place it.", "GUIDA": "The door into all of it, free for everyone with no monthly cap. Describe the problem and it names the specialist.", "ANALISI": "Reads key, tempo and provenance from a file or a whole folder, then listens to the audio and writes what it hears back into it.", "SAPIENZA": "AIUTO's architecture pointed at a different library: vetted professional guides on the craft itself, rather than one application's manual."};
const toolDescriptions={"SCORE CONVERTER": "Turns MuseScore files into clean MusicXML that any notation app opens, or a Standard MIDI file. It also swaps MusicXML and MIDI. One file or a whole batch.", "SCORE VIEWER": "Drop a MuseScore, MusicXML or MIDI file and read it in the page, with its note count and stats up top. Export what you are looking at as PDF.", "MEDIA CONVERTER": "WAV and MP3, mono/stereo mixing and level normalising. One file or a whole batch, converted on your machine, nothing uploaded.", "ANALISI": "Key, tempo, duration, and every scrap of embedded metadata a file carries: who made it, in what software, when it last changed.", "SAPIENZA": "Ask about ranges, transposition, doublings and balance and get the answer in the page. The free front door to the SAPIENZA specialist.", "ISOLATOR": "A memo, a dialogue take, an interview: the voice comes back clean, separated from the room around it. Included with your free account.", "CURIOSITIES": "Orchestra history, instruments, notation, film scoring. Tap the sphere and it deals a fact, with no repeats until the deck runs out."};
